Negative control for the Code sheet never printing harness code (`R7-6`).

Puts the step-runner back into the snippet. The pane keeps printing the real
composable call — the scope, the criteria, the actions — and simply boots the
harness world above it, which is exactly the regression `R7-6` overturns: while
a track was armed the pane used to print what the SCENARIO executes rather than
what a developer would write. One line is enough to re-cross that line, because
the law is absolute: the reader is a developer copying the call into their own
app, and `useScenarioWorld` is not something they can call.

Nothing else moves — the scope builder, the filter/sort serialisation, the copy
path and the markdown fence are untouched — so a red here is the law and not a
crash or a formatting drift.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: code-pane.spec.ts — the case asserting the fence carries the composable's
own call and nothing else, and any case asserting the snippet names no harness
or step-runner symbol (`useScenarioWorld`, `world`, a Gherkin `Given`/`When`/
`Then` line), armed or live. The scope, filter and sort cases stay GREEN under
the mutant, by construction; if they go red too, the control has been
over-applied.

  FOR THE PROVER: authored by the developer seat, which knew the line to mutate;
  it carries no verification run. Apply it blind, confirm the harness-code case
